    "title": "Ambispective Evaluation of the Sentinel Patch in Adults With Postoperative Pain",
    "background": "Postoperative pain outcomes are captured inconsistently across historical records and prospective follow-up, limiting interpretation of recovery patterns.",
    "hypothesis": "Combined historical records and prospective follow-up will show measurable improvement in pain tracking completeness by Month 3.",
    "timeline": "Historical record review plus prospective baseline through Month 3 follow-up, with prospective participation lasting approximately 14 weeks.",
